<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-douady-magnetic-drop-phyllotaxis> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Douady & Couder (1992, 1996) self-organized magnetic-drop phyllotaxis & imperfect pitchfork cascade (Pinus sp. conifer seed cone & botanical shoot apical meristem (SAM))",
        "Douady & Couder (1992, 1996) self-organized magnetic-drop phyllotaxis & imperfect pitchfork cascade faithfully reproduces Pinus sp. conifer seed cone & botanical shoot apical meristem (SAM) morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/douady-magnetic-drop-phyllotaxis-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/douady-magnetic-drop-phyllotaxis-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/douady-magnetic-drop-phyllotaxis-3> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) 1992-douady-magnetic-drop-phyllotaxis.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Pinus sp. conifer seed cone & botanical shoot apical meristem (SAM) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 91.0/100, audit 2026-10-19-magnetic-drop-phyllotaxis-audit-v2) and the assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/317bc3c/1992-douady-magnetic-drop-phyllotaxis.py> ;
    schema:about "Pinus sp. conifer seed cone & botanical shoot apical meristem (SAM)" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Subcellular PIN1 polar auxin efflux carrier trafficking or continuous reaction-diffusion PDE dynamics on the meristem (covered in Slot 033 Jönsson et al. 2006 / Smith et al. 2006)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Difference-of-Gaussians (DoG) scale-umbo segmentation (N = 123 scales) and log-polar (u = ln r, theta) 2D FFT spiral spectrum extraction confirming opposing (m_CW, m_CCW) = (5, 8) Fibonacci parastichies on `conifer_cone_specimen.jpg`",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Exact 2-drop and full-chain Hessian fold (G_fold = 0.773484 exp / 2.514560 lin) and dynamical pitchfork (G_c1 = 0.860537 exp / 3.631432 lin) roots, regular-spiral zero-force equilibrium locus F(G, dphi) = 0, and adiabatic continuation along both Fibonacci (r = 0.99999, RMSE = 0.065 deg) and Lucas (RMSE = 0.141 deg) branches",
        "reported_in_source: Douady & Couder (1992) Fig. 3 & (1996) J. Theor. Biol. 178:255-274 supercritical (1,1)->(1,2) pitchfork bifurcation and imperfect pitchfork cascade along the Fibonacci branch (1,2,3,5,8,13) -> 137.508 deg and disconnected Lucas branch (1,3,4,7,11) -> 99.502 deg",
        "reported_in_source: Douady & Couder (1992) Phys. Rev. Lett. 68:2098-2101 iterative magnetic-dipole repulsion energy E(phi) = sum_{k>=1} d_k(phi, phi_{n-k})^{-3} on a circular rim r = R_0 controlled by dimensionless plastochron ratio G = V * T / R_0",
        "transfer_boundary: 2D planar/conical projection of radial meristem advection r_k = R_0 * exp(k*G) and silicone-oil ferrofluid dish advection r_k = R_0 * (1 + k*G) mapped onto apical conifer cone scale lattices" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "4. Polar Auxin & Turgor Stress" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "III. Phyta (Embryophyta)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Spirals, Veins & Puzzle Cells" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Golden Angle / Auxin Flux" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Angiospermae & Gymnospermae" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Helianthus" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/317bc3c/1992-douady-magnetic-drop-phyllotaxis.py; output: docs/media/magnetic_drop_phyllotaxis_comparison.png; organism: Pinus sp. conifer seed cone & botanical shoot apical meristem (SAM); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/317bc3c; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1; spec_fingerprint: 33eddc6c7f7154d2ce87a1a999bc4ec67c98aaa43e0d2412fb26a2fc20bc5041; artifact_sha256: 779d9de0700bbef59454bf311549f619c754aa2ee9d124d3e314546ea02b7e79; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/magnetic_drop_phyllotaxis/conifer_cone_specimen.jpg=7bcb68e856d4db53..., datasets/magnetic_drop_phyllotaxis/magnetic_drop_phyllotaxis_reference.json=9ae33106a0fea23f..., datasets/magnetic_drop_phyllotaxis/paper_citations.bib=2c3aa1ec0e4c53de...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-magnetic-drop-phyllotaxis-audit; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Douady & Couder (1992) Phys. Rev. Lett. 68:2098-2101 iterative magnetic-dipole repulsion energy E(phi) = sum_{k>=1} d_k(phi, phi_{n-k})^{-3} on a circular rim r = R_0 controlled by dimensionless plastochron ratio G = V * T / R_0 | Douady & Couder (1992) Fig. 3 & (1996) J. Theor. Biol. 178:255-274 supercritical (1,1)->(1,2) pitchfork bifurcation and imperfect pitchfork cascade along the Fibonacci branch (1,2,3,5,8,13) -> 137.508 deg and disconnected Lucas branch (1,3,4,7,11) -> 99.502 deg; reconstructed_in_script: Exact 2-drop and full-chain Hessian fold (G_fold = 0.773484 exp / 2.514560 lin) and dynamical pitchfork (G_c1 = 0.860537 exp / 3.631432 lin) roots, regular-spiral zero-force equilibrium locus F(G, dphi) = 0, and adiabatic continuation along both Fibonacci (r = 0.99999, RMSE = 0.065 deg) and Lucas (RMSE = 0.141 deg) branches | Difference-of-Gaussians (DoG) scale-umbo segmentation (N = 123 scales) and log-polar (u = ln r, theta) 2D FFT spiral spectrum extraction confirming opposing (m_CW, m_CCW) = (5, 8) Fibonacci parastichies on `conifer_cone_specimen.jpg`; transfer_boundary: 2D planar/conical projection of radial meristem advection r_k = R_0 * exp(k*G) and silicone-oil ferrofluid dish advection r_k = R_0 * (1 + k*G) mapped onto apical conifer cone scale lattices; does_not_claim: Subcellular PIN1 polar auxin efflux carrier trafficking or continuous reaction-diffusion PDE dynamics on the meristem (covered in Slot 033 Jönsson et al. 2006 / Smith et al. 2006)]" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1006/jtbi.1996.0024>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1006/jtbi.1996.0025>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.68.2098>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1209/0295-5075/14/6/006> ;
